{
  "dom_id": "step-26435",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Suppose that we have a cube whose edges are $2\\,\\textrm{cm}$ in length, like the one shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242839/assets/b974b6e782801fbe2099971afd0df9a5c6e05a10afc2ce0e4054c850088e753b.png)\n\nThe formula for the volume $V$ of a cube with sides of length $s$ is given by\n\n$$\nV = s^3.\n$$\n\nTo find the volume of this cube, we substitute $s=2 \\: \\textrm{cm}$ into the formula. This gives\n\n$$\nV = (2\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 8 \\text{ cm}^3 .\n$$\n\nSo the volume of the cube is $8\\,\\textrm{cm}^3.$",
